"white-space:nowrap\">Term</th><th>Grammar topics (JKBOSE syllabus)</th></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Term I</td><td>Punctuation Marks • Tenses • Narration (Direct → Indirect) • Using Words as Parts of Speech</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Term II</td><td>Phrases • Subject-Verb Agreement • Editing a Passage based on Tenses • Passives (Active → Passive) • Use of Articles, Adjectives and Adverbs</td></tr></table></div></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\">\n    <div class=\"q-title\">✦ Section B: Grammar — How You Are Tested (5 Marks each term)</div><div class=\"sol-step\"><div class=\"rev\">In both terms, <b>Section B carries 5 marks</b>. The syllabus says that <b>contextualised passages</b> will be given for editing — that is, you will get a short paragraph with mistakes and must correct them.</div><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"dt\"><colgroup><col style=\"width:22%\"><col style=\"width:78%\"></colgroup><tr><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Term</th><th>Passages test…</th></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Term I</td><td>tenses, punctuation, narration and different parts of speech</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Term II</td><td>tenses, passives, subject-verb agreement, articles and different parts of speech</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"pt\"><b>So:</b> learn each rule, then practise spotting it inside a passage. Every tab in the Q &amp; A section gives you the rules first, then exam-style practice with answers.</div></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\">\n    <div class=\"q-title\">✦ Quick-Revision Golden Rules</div><div class=\"sol-step\"><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Punctuation:</span> capital letter at the start and for names; a comma before the inverted commas; the question mark goes <i>inside</i> the inverted commas.</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Tenses:</span> time words are your clue — <i>yesterday</i> → past, <i>since/for</i> → present perfect (continuous), <i>tomorrow</i> → future.</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Narration:</span> past reporting verb → move the tense one step back; change pronouns and 'near' words (now → then, here → there).</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Parts of speech:</span> a word's job in the sentence decides its part of speech — 'light' can be a noun, verb or adjective.</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Phrases:</span> a group of words without its own subject and verb, doing the job of a noun, adjective or adverb.</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Agreement:</span> singular subject → singular verb (<i>he goes</i>); plural subject → plural verb (<i>they go</i>).</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Passives:</span> object becomes subject + <b>be</b> + past participle (+ by …).</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Articles:</span> <i>a/an</i> depends on the first <b>sound</b>, not the letter: <i>an hour, a university</i>.</div><div class=\"pt\"><span class=\"lbl\">Adjective vs adverb:</span> adjectives describe nouns (<i>a careful driver</i>); adverbs describe verbs (<i>drives carefully</i>).</div></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\">\n    <div class=\"q-title\">✦ How to Use This Module</div><div class=\"sol-step\"><div class=\"pt\">Open <b>Q &amp; A</b>, choose <b>Term - I</b> or <b>Term - II</b>, then pick a topic tab.</div><div class=\"pt\">Read the <b>rules and examples</b> card first, then try each practice question yourself before reading the answer.</div><div class=\"pt\">The <b>Editing</b> tab (Term - II) gives full exam-style passages — do these last, as revision.</div><div class=\"pt\">Writing Skills (letters, notices, dialogues and more) are in the next module, <b>Writing Skills &amp; Formats</b>.</div><div class=\"exam\"><span class=\"exam-t\">📌 Exam Focus</span><div>• Punctuating dialogue correctly</div><div>• Choosing the right tense from time clues</div><div>• Direct → indirect speech (statements, questions, commands)</div><div>• Active → passive in all main tenses</div><div>• Subject-verb agreement with each, either/neither, one of</div><div>• Editing a passage line by line</div></div></div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>",
